      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Practice - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor of Practice - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor of Practice 538292 Blacksburg, Virginia Business Information Technology Teaching & Research Faculty College of Business Job Description The Department of Business Information Technology in the R. B. Pamplin College of Business at Virginia Tech invites applications for a non tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Practice. Duties will include teaching information technology (IT), business analytics, supply chain management or cybersecurity courses at the undergraduate and graduate level. The teaching load will be 24 credit hours per year. Other duties may include participation in departmental committees, and activities including advising and mentoring students as assigned by the department head. Occasional travel may be required to attend professional meetings and conferences. The Department of Business Information Technology in the R. B. Pamplin College of Business at Virginia Tech invites applications for a non tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Practice. Duties will include teaching information technology (IT), business analytics, supply chain management or cybersecurity courses at the undergraduate and graduate level. The teaching load will be 24 credit hours per year. Other duties may include participation in departmental committees, and activities including advising and mentoring students as assigned by the department head. Occasional travel may be required to attend professional meetings and conferences. Responsibilities include: •Teach and develop undergraduate and/or graduate courses within the Department of Business Information Technology curriculum. •Provide academic leadership and mentorship within the department. •Contribute to departmental, college, and university service and governance. •Support the strategic growth and visibility of the department’s academic programs and initiatives. About the Department: The Department of Business Information Technology upholds a strong commitment to academic excellence, innovative research, and meaningful engagement in service across the department, college, and university. Our faculty pursue high impact research endeavors and foster an enriching and supportive educational environment. Additional details about the department can be found at www.bit.vt.edu. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in business administration, business analytics, supply chain management, information technology (IT) or related field; job-related experience in IT, cybersecurity, analytics or supply chain; effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in supply chain, management science, IS or IT-related field. Professional certifications in IT, analytics, cybersecurity or supply chain management. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information Starting at $125k; commensurate with experience Hours per week N/A Review Date 11/6/2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Adrienne Sable at asable@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 5b982edb Last Name (required) 2b11ba75 Email (required) 437ef58d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank yo