    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/associate-or-full-professor-blacksburg-virginia-united-states-14df5d03-72b9-46f0-9f22-ec54c33f6be3": {
      "title": "Associate or Full Professor",
      "description": "Associate or Full Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Associate or Full Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Associate or Full Professor 538295 Blacksburg, Virginia Blackwood Department of Real Estate Teaching & Research Faculty College of Business Job Description The Blackwood Department of Real Estate within the R. B. Pamplin College of Business at Virginia Tech invites applications for an Associate or Full Professor of Real Estate who will hold the Blackwood Endowed Chair. This is an exciting opportunity for an established scholar to join a growing department interested in expanding its research, teaching, and service capacity while continuing to build its international reputation. The position is a tenured, academic-year appointment beginning August 10, 2027. The successful candidate will conduct high-quality research regularly leading to publications in top-tier academic journals such as Journal of Real Estate Finance and Economics, Journal of Real Estate Research, and Real Estate Economics. Additionally, the candidate will carry an annual teaching load of three courses (9 credits) in the undergraduate real estate program and engage in service activities that increase awareness of the department in both the academic and professional communities. Instructional effectiveness and flexibility are essential, as is a willingness to engage in experiential learning activities that prepare undergraduate students for their eventual entry into the workforce. Responsibilities include: · Conduct high-quality research leading to publication in top-tier academic journals. · Teach three courses (9 credits) annually in the undergraduate real estate program. · Engage in experiential learning activities that prepare undergraduate students for entry into the workforce. · Participate in service activities that increase awareness of the department within academic and professional communities. · Explore emerging real estate trends, present at national and international conferences, engage in timely policy debate, and contribute to the professionalization of the real estate industry. · Contribute to the Pamplin+ initiative, with its focus on technology readiness and workforce preparation. · Work collegially and collaboratively with faculty and staff. About the Department: Thanks to a generous $10 million gift from the Blackwood family in 2021, the department’s endowment is well positioned to support the scholarly endeavors of its faculty. Faculty are encouraged to explore emerging real estate trends, present at national and international conferences, engage in timely policy debate, and contribute to the professionalization of the real estate industry at large. At present, the department serves approximately 400 undergraduate students pursuing B.S. Real Estate degrees who complete a core business curriculum coupled with a series of courses introducing them to the fundamentals of real estate development, finance, law, market analysis, operations, and planning. The curriculum also provides students with opportunities to pursue double majors or minors in real estate-adjacent fields while still graduating within four years. As one of seven departments in the Pamplin College of Business, the Blackwood Department of Real Estate and its faculty contribute to the Pamplin+ initiative, which focuses on technology readiness and workforce preparation from the time students enroll in the college until the time they graduate. Faculty are also expected to demonstrate a willingness to work collegially and collaboratively with faculty and staff. Additional information about the department is available at: https://realestate.vt.edu/index.html Required Qualifications Ph.D. in real estate or related discipline from an accredited institution by the date of initial appointment (Equivalent foreign degrees are acceptable). Research record indicating a nationally/internationally recognized and well developed research program. Occasional travel to attend conferences and meetings. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level in multiple real estate or real estate-related courses. Evidence of engagement with professional real estate societies, organizations, or industry associations. Experience mentoring junior faculty, early-career scholars, or other academic colleagues. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information Commensurate with experience Review Date 11/02/2026; open until filled Additional Information Occasional travel to attend conferences and meetings The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Stephanie Hairston at steph316@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 7425f9ca Last Name (required) d4bb9ca1 Email (required) 88b7246c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 230d7d39 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Business College of Business First Name (required) f189609b Last Name 