    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-in-experimental-space-physics-and-radar-remote-sensing-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Experimental Space Physics and Radar Remote Sensing",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Experimental Space Physics and Radar Remote Sensing - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant or Associate Professor in Experimental Space Physics and Radar Remote Sensing - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant or Associate Professor in Experimental Space Physics and Radar Remote Sensing 538285 Blacksburg, Virginia Electrical and ComputerEngineering Teaching & Research Faculty College of Engineering Job Description The Bradley Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Experimental Space Physics and Radar Remote Sensing, with an anticipated start date of August 2027. The position is expected to be filled at the rank of assistant or associate professor. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in electrical engineering, space physics, or a closely related field. Candidates should show strong potential for excellence in undergraduate instruction, specialized graduate education, externally sponsored research, and scholarly activity. The ECE Department includes nearly 100 faculty members, more than 500 full-time graduate students, and more than 1,000 undergraduate students. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching in areas aligned with experimental space physics and radar remote sensing, as well as other related ECE topics such as satellite communications, electromagnetics, antennas and RF propagation. Candidates may also participate in the Interdisciplinary Graduate Education Program in Remote Sensing (http://rsigep.frec.vt.edu) which spans multiple departments and colleges across the university. The successful candidate will also be expected to contribute to departmental, college, and university service and to mentor students in a manner consistent with Virginia Tech’s Principles of Community. The successful applicant will contribute to the University’s Center for Space Science and Engineering Research (Space@VT, http://www.space.vt.edu) which brings together faculty, students, and partners across space science, remote sensing, satellite systems, and space engineering. Its research facilities support a broad portfolio of experimental and computational research, with the Super Dual Auroral Radar Network (SuperDARN) Space Weather Radar Facility serving as an important component of a broader set of research capabilities. SuperDARN provides key observations of Earth’s near-space environment, and Virginia Tech is a PI institution in the international SuperDARN collaboration, which operates a worldwide network of HF space weather radars. In addition to Space@VT, further research resources and opportunities for collaboration are available through the Institute for Critical Technology and Applied Science (http://www.ictas.vt.edu), the National Security Institute (https://nationalsecurity.vt.edu) and Virginia Tech Advanced Research Computing (http://www.arc.vt.edu). Virginia Tech is a comprehensive land-grant university guided by its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), with a strong emphasis on hands-on, transdisciplinary learning, discovery, and problem-solving. The university enrolls more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students across more than 280 majors and multiple colleges and professional schools. Based in Blacksburg with additional locations across Virginia, Virginia Tech is also a leading global research institution, with more than $500 million in annual research activity. Virginia Tech is an equal opportunity employer. The university is committed to building a culturally diverse faculty and strongly encourages applications from candidates who will contribute to inclusive excellence in research, teaching, and service. Applicants are required to apply online at https://jobs.vt.edu/ and should use posting number 538285. Application materials should include a cover letter, a current CV, contact information for three professional references, and statements describing research, teaching, and professional goals . Questions about the search process may be directed to Dr. Joseph Baker, Faculty Search Committee Chair, Bradley Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, at jo.baker@vt.edu. Review of applications will begin November 30, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Space Physics, Applied Physics, or a closely related field by the appointment start date. Demonstrated research experience in experimental space physics, radar remote sensing, ionospheric physics, space weather, or a closely related field. Evidence of scholarly productivity or potential through peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, or other recognized research contributions. Demonstrated ability or potential to develop an externally funded research program, as evidenced by research proposals, sponsored research participation, or a clearly articulated research agenda. Demonstrated ability or potential to teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students in electrical and computer engineering or related disciplines. Preferred Qualifications Research experience involving high-frequency (HF) radar systems, ionospheric remote sensing, or space weather observations. Experience with the design, development, operation, or analysis of radar and remote sensing systems, including SuperDARN or comparable observational networks. Record of peer-reviewed scholarly publications in experimental space physics, radar remote sensing, or related disciplines. Experience securing or contributing to externally sponsored research funding from federal agencies, industry partners, or other research sponsors. Experience teaching undergraduate or graduate courses in electromagnetics, antennas, RF propagation, satellite communications, or related ECE subjects. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information $110,000–$150,000 Hours per week 40 Review Date November 30, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Cole Tankersley at cpt19@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 5d6c6721 Last Name (required) d7abb508 Email (required) 6f417317 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 4e01d531 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Engineering Instructional / Teaching Faculty Research / Scientific Engineering Instructional / Teaching Faculty Research / Scientific Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Engineering College of Engineering First Name (required) a3753ec7 Last Name (required) d5f9a405 Email (required) e18db5f3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 5bce714b Last Name (required) b3610295 Email (required) 768b4aaa Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Agricultural Technician-Suffolk, VA Suffolk Virginia Tidewater AREC Virginia Tech's Tidewater Agricultural Research and Extension Center (AREC) is seeking a dedicated and detail-oriented Research Technician to assist our dynamic field crops agronomy and soybean research program. This is an off-campus, part-time position located at our facility in Suffolk, Virginia. You will work under the direction of the Agricultural Supervisor to support the lifecycle of small-plot agricultural research, from seed packaging to precision planting, field data collection, and post-harvest quality analysis. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - Northampton Machiponogo, Virginia Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for Northampton County. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - York County Yorktown Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for York County. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a senior management"
