    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/clinical-instructor-for-emergency-medicine-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor for Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor for Emergency Medicine - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Clinical Instructor for Emergency Medicine - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Clinical Instructor for Emergency Medicine 538194 Blacksburg, Virginia Small Animal Clinical Sciences Teaching & Research Faculty College of Veterinary Medicine Job Description Do you enjoy practicing high-quality, evidence-based clinical medicine along with the opportunity to educate the next generation of veterinarians? Are you looking for a more fulfilling career path? Consider applying for a clinical instructor position with the emergency and critical care service at Virginia Tech. The Department of Small Animal Clinical Sciences at the Virginia-Maryland College of Veterinary Medicine (VMCVM) is seeking a full-time emergency veterinarian. This position is a Clinical Instructor appointment with expectations of clinical teaching and primary case responsibility, as well as a limited amount of classroom and laboratory instruction. The Emergency & Critical Care Service (ECC) is a rapidly growing service at the VMCVM with three criticalists, three emergency veterinarians, ECC residents, and rotating interns, all supported by a highly qualified team of experienced veterinary technicians. The emergency clinician can expect to learn from and collaborate with veterinarians throughout the hospital. At the same time, our clinicians help develop the next generation of veterinarians by supporting our veterinary students during the highly-rated ECC clerkship The experienced emergency clinician in this role will be expected to oversee the clinical education of veterinary students, interns, and residents. Oversight of timely, accurate triage and outpatient care for all cases arriving on emergency with primary case responsibility for ~50% of cases that are presented, dependent upon caseload and complexity. Inpatient care through oversight of interns, collaboration with criticalists, and occasionally primary care dependent on caseload should be expected. Support from a criticalist is dependably available through consultation and co-management of cases. Day and swing shifts are expected, with occasional on-call/back-up shifts to support interns during their overnight shifts. For clinicians with surgical interest, additional compensation can be earned by performing after-hours surgeries Benefits (https://www.hr.vt.edu/benefits.html): • Competitive academic salary • Student loan repayment support • Signing bonus • Annual leave • Health insurance eligibility • Pre-load annual leave to use at the start of the position • Thousands of Hokie discounts managed by PerkSpot Starting Date: • Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026, and will continue until a candidate is appointed. Application: • Interested candidates should apply online at jobs.vt.edu (click on Current Job Openings, Search by Department – Small Animal Clinical Sciences) • If you experience difficulties applying online, please contact Courtney Snead at csnead@vt.edu Required Qualifications • DVM or equivalent foreign degree by appointment start date • Must be eligible for a Virginia faculty veterinary license by appointment start date • Experience in small animal emergency medicine and/or successful completion of a small animal rotating internship, by appointment start date • Excellent communication skills and interpersonal interactions • Commitment to diversity and inclusion • Demonstrated interest in education and/or clinical instruction Preferred Qualifications • Substantial clinical experience • Surgical experience • Advanced emergency training • Teaching experience Pay Band Faculty; Salary Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information Salary; Commensurate with experience Hours per week 40+ Review Date November 1, 2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Dr. Bobbi Conner at bobbiconner@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 95f4aa9c Last Name (required) 1b4048bd Email (required) 63b08913 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert a28b9e1e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Veterinary Medicine Veterinary Medicine Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Veterinary Medicine College of Veterinary Medicine First Name (required) d0c4ee02 Last Name (required) 43a9fb31 Email (required) c17ef12a Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 190f9bf2 Last Name (required) 87eba82a Email (required) d562741a Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Agricultural Technician-Suffolk, VA Suffolk Virginia Tidewater AREC Virginia Tech's Tidewater Agricultural Research and Extension Center (AREC) is seeking a dedicated and detail-oriented Research Technician to assist our dynamic field crops agronomy and soybean research program. This is an off-campus, part-time position located at our facility in Suffolk, Virginia. You will work under the direction of the Agricultural Supervisor to support the lifecycle of small-plot agricultural research, from seed packaging to precision planting, field data collection, and post-harvest quality analysis. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - Northampton Machiponogo, Virginia Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for Northampton County. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - York County Yorktown Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for York County. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies