    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-agricultural-markets-trade-and-rural-development-policy-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Agricultural Markets, Trade, and Rural Development Policy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Agricultural Markets, Trade, and Rural Development Policy - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor, Agricultural Markets, Trade, and Rural Development Policy - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor, Agricultural Markets, Trade, and Rural Development Policy 538120 Blacksburg, Virginia Agricultural & Applied Economics Teaching & Research Faculty Agriculture & Life Sciences Job Description The Department of Agricultural and Applied Economics (AAEC) in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) invites applications for a tenure-track position in agricultural markets, trade, and rural development policy. This is a 9-month, academic-year appointment, with expectations to fund summer activities through external grants or other mechanisms. The specific appointment is 50 percent research and 50 percent Extension. The successful candidate will maintain a visible, nationally recognized, externally funded applied research and Extension program in agricultural markets, trade, and rural development policy analysis, with a particular focus on distilling and successfully communicating the impacts of proposed policies and market changes to stakeholders across the Commonwealth of Virginia. International engagement and recognition are encouraged and expected as the candidate’s career advances. The successful candidate is expected to collaborate with colleagues in AAEC, the Center for Agricultural Trade, and other departments in CALS to develop effective Extension and applied research programs that integrate market, policy, and trade analysis into existing efforts on local food systems and rural development initiatives. This position will also work closely with Extension agents, specialists, and field staff to develop effective and visible programs. By collaborating with others in the department, CALS, across campus and beyond, the successful candidate will serve as a catalyst for interdisciplinary activity, bridging the technical rigor of quantitative analysis with the practical, applied focus of Extension work needed to address the market, trade, and policy impacts confronting rural communities in Virginia. Through dissemination of trade and policy impacts, this position will enhance communication and public policy outreach efforts in CALS that foster economic growth and resilience in our rural communities. As a priority to develop and foster new partnerships and leverage existing ones across campus and the commonwealth, the candidate is expected to build partnerships with stakeholders (e.g. government, industry, nonprofits, etc.), producer groups, agricultural lenders, supply chain businesses, and others. The position will also enhance communication to raise awareness of CALS engagement in the communities we serve. There is an expectation of excellence in grantsmanship, timely communication of research findings through publication in peer-reviewed journal articles and extension outlets, and mentoring students. This position requires occasional travel for meetings and conferences. The Department of Agricultural and Applied Economics (https://aaec.vt.edu/) is a growing unit with approximately 250 undergraduate students, 45 graduate students, and 27 faculty members. The department offers unique opportunities to develop applied research and outreach programs that have meaningful impacts on decision-makers. The department offers undergraduate programs in agribusiness and applied economic management (https://aaec.vt.edu/academics/undergraduate.html), an online and in-person Master’s program, and a joint Ph.D. with the Department of Economics (https://aaec.vt.edu/academics/graduate.html). The department collaborates closely with other units within the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences, as well as with various units on campus. The Department is located in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (http://www.cals.vt.edu/), which has about 2,600 undergraduate students and 600 graduate students across 10 academic units. The Virginia Agricultural Experiment Station and Virginia Cooperative Extension, within the college, deliver research-based information to the Commonwealth of Virginia through county/city extension offices, 4-H educational centers, and Agricultural Research and Extension Centers (http://www.ext.vt.edu/offices). About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges, a school of medicine, a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School, and Honors College. The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes. A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance. These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. Required Qualifications • Ph,D, in Agricultural Economics, Applied Economics, Agribusiness, Regional Science, or a closely related discipline by appointment start date. • Demonstrated ability (or potential) for publishing peer-reviewed research, Extension, and teaching materials. • Skills in and experience applying regional economic and international trade models in conducting economic analysis. • Demonstrated ability (or potential) in communicating and synthesizing complex economic analyses to a wide range of audiences. Preferred Qualifications • Experience developing and delivering economic-based educational programs to extension agents, business managers, industry groups, public agency personnel, and stakeholders. • Experience applying for grants or other funding for programmatic support, including running fee-based workshops, and/or establishing novel sources of external funding to support integrated research or Extension programs. • Experience working with clientele such as industry partners, commodity groups, and government agencies. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information $85,000 - $110,000; commensurate with experience Hours per week 40; M-F 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Review Date 11/29/2026 Additional Information Application packets should include: a. A formal cover letter summarizing qualifications, b. a statement describing Research and Extension philosophy (2-pg max), d. a current curriculum vitae, and e. the names and contact information of three professional references who can assess the applicant’s qualifications for this position. The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Dr. Jason Grant at jhgrant@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) cff34d84 Last Name (required) 5f044cc3 Email (required) 597143b8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 9580b641 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture / Life Science Agriculture / Life Science Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Agriculture & Life Sciences Agriculture & Life Sciences First Name (required) 6f54b48e Last Name (required) 6fea2084 Email (required) aa7e3b7d Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 20fb1bfa Last Name (required) 207800d3 Email (required) 57968471 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messag