    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-in-technical-and-scientific-communication-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Technical and Scientific Communication",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Technical and Scientific Communication - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant/Associate Professor in Technical and Scientific Communication - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant/Associate Professor in Technical and Scientific Communication 538128 Blacksburg, Virginia English Teaching & Research Faculty Liberal Arts and Human Sciences Job Description Virginia Tech’s Department of English invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in Technical and Scientific Communication. This position reflects Virginia Tech's strategic commitment to understanding not only how technologies are developed, but how they are implemented, communicated, trusted, and integrated into organizations and communities, with a particular focus on healthcare. We seek an innovative scholar whose work advances the future of technical and scientific communication in an era increasingly defined by artificial intelligence, automation, immersive technologies, and complex sociotechnical systems. We seek a scholar whose research and teaching examine how communication shapes the design, implementation, and use of emerging technologies in professional, organizational, scientific, technical, or healthcare environments. This position is associated with Virginia Tech’s Smart Healthcare Hub initiative (smarthealthcare.icat.vt.edu) and will contribute to the growth of interdisciplinary research, innovation, and teaching at the intersection of emerging technologies, healthcare-related simulations, digital and/or medical humanities, experience design, operations, and human-centered systems. The successful candidate will join a highly multidisciplinary and collaborative environment that values innovation, experiential learning, translational research, and community engagement. The successful candidate will contribute to Virginia Tech's internationally recognized Technical and Scientific Communication program as a member of the Department of English while engaging in interdisciplinary research collaborations across the university. Given the expectation that the position will involve high research productivity and pursuit of research funding as part of the Smart Healthcare Hub initiative, the position will begin with a teaching assignment of two courses per academic year (one in fall and one in spring) that includes teaching in the Department of English’s undergraduate Technical and Scientific Communication and the doctoral Rhetoric and Writing programs. After three years, the teaching assignment is expected to increase to the department’s typical teaching assignment for tenure-track and tenured faculty of four courses each academic year (two in fall and two in spring). Position Overview The ideal candidate for this position will help define the future of the discipline by advancing research that improves communication across complex technical, scientific, healthcare, governmental, or industrial contexts. We welcome applicants whose scholarship addresses one or more areas including, but not limited to: Ethics of emerging technologies Rhetoric of science, technology, and medicine Digital and/or medical humanities Human-centered design Technical communication and artificial intelligence Accessibility and inclusive design Science writing The department particularly values scholars whose work bridges traditional disciplinary boundaries and who are skilled at collaborating with researchers across engineering, computer science, health sciences, business, public policy, and the humanities. We seek an individual that has expertise in applying their work within the healthcare sector. Responsibilities The successful candidate will maintain an active, externally visible research program, including work associated with the Smart Healthcare Hub’s focus; contribute to undergraduate and graduate education; mentor students; and participate in departmental, college, and university service. Primary responsibilities include: Research Develop and sustain a nationally recognized program of scholarship in technical and scientific communication. Publish in leading journals and present research at national and international conferences. Pursue externally funded research opportunities and contribute to collaborative external funding proposals. Build interdisciplinary collaborations across Virginia Tech and with external partners. Mentor graduate and undergraduate student researchers. Teaching Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in technical and scientific communication and rhetoric, including foundational and advanced courses that may include grant writing; medical and science writing; the rhetoric of science, technology, and medicine; document design; visual rhetoric; and/or digital rhetoric. Faculty are encouraged to develop new courses aligned with their expertise and emerging areas of the discipline. Service The successful candidate will contribute to the continued growth of Virginia Tech's nationally recognized Technical and Scientific Communication program through curriculum development, student mentoring, program leadership, and university service while participating in national professional organizations. Collaborative Opportunities Virginia Tech offers exceptional opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. The successful candidate will have opportunities to engage with faculty across the College of Liberal Arts and Human Sciences, College of Engineering, College of Science, Virginia Tech Carilion School of Medicine, Pamplin College of Business, and numerous university-wide research institutes and centers such as the Institute for Society, Culture, and Environment, Institute for Creativity, Arts, and Technology, the Fralin Biomedical Research Institute, and the Whole Health Consortium. How to Apply Screening of applications will begin November 15, 2026. For full consideration, all materials must be submitted prior to this date. Please submit: A CV A Cover Letter A detailed statement detailing teaching/mentoring philosophy A detailed statement of research accomplishments and plans Names and contact information for 3 professional references; references will be contacted to upload letters of support to the application during the review process Please direct questions to Dr. James D. Ivory, Search Committee Chair, at jivory@vt.edu . Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Technical and Professional Communication, Rhetoric and Writing Studies, Communication, English, Information Science, Human-Centered Computing, Science Communication, User Experience, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Demonstrated potential for an active and impactful research agenda supported by extramural funding. Evidence of excellence or strong potential in undergraduate and graduate teaching. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive teaching, mentoring, and collaboration. Ability to work effectively in interdisciplinary research environments. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with one or more of the following: Research addressing emerging technologies and communication. Expertise in human-centered design, user experience, or information design. Research focused on healthcare, health technologies, public health, or implementation. Evidence of pursuing or securing external research funding. Experience mentoring graduate students. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information Commensurate with Experience, as an Assistant Professor the range is $75,000 to $82,000 / as an Associate Professor the range is $83,000 to $92,000 Hours per week * Review Date November 15, 2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Donna Eastwood at ddolgos@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 5982b34c Last Name (required) ccdba06a Email (required) ba19dbdd Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 6b5c38ea Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Liberal Arts and Human Sciences Liberal Arts and Human Sciences First Name (required) ad0983f3 Last Name (required) cff8d47f Email (required) a3dea7f5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) bade9dd8 Last Name (required) 027c81e1 Email (required) 479b98f6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Agricultural Technician-Suffolk, VA Suffolk Virginia Tidewater AREC Virginia Tech's Tidewater Agricultural Research and Extension Center (AREC) is seeking a dedicated and detail-oriented Research Technician to assist our dynamic field crops agronomy and soybean research program. This is an off-campus, part-time position located at our facility in Suffolk, Virginia. You will work under the direction of the Agricultural Supervisor to support the lifecycle of small-plot agricultural research, from seed packaging to precision planting, field data collection, and post-harvest quality analysis. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - Northampton Machiponogo, Virginia Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for Northampton County. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - York County Yorktown Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for York County. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a senior