      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Postdoctoral Associate - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Postdoctoral Associate 538232 Blacksburg, Virginia Biological Systems Engineering Research Faculty Agriculture & Life Sciences Job Description The Department of Biological Systems Engineering at Virginia Tech is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate. The project will focus on “preclinical evaluation of engineered drug and gene delivery systems”. Nanoformulations or devices will be engineered for enhancing the efficacy and safety of biologically active drugs and gene therapies. The selected individual will work with Dr. Wujin Sun and a team of researchers at Virginia Tech. The selected individual will lead in vivo efficacy and safety studies, bioimaging, and histological analysis. Required Qualifications - PhD must be awarded no more than four years prior to the effective date of the appointment with a minimum of one year eligibility remaining in physiology, pharmacology, immunology, bioengineering, biomedical engineering, veterinary or biomedical sciences, biological systems engineering, or related scientific or engineering field - Self-motivated individual who shows initiative and creativity - Effective communication skills Preferred Qualifications - Experience with in vivo animal studies, including rodent handling and treatment administration - Experience with mouse models of disease or of wound healing and tissue repair - Experience with intravital, confocal, or two-photon microscopy - Experience with histology and immunofluorescence analysis - Experience with drug delivery Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information $53,550-$65,029; commensurate with experience Hours per week 40 Review Date 11/03/2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Dr. Wujin Sun at sunw@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) c89a3acd Last Name (required) c30cfb20 Email (required) 2dddc79b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 6c8372a8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture / Life Science Research / Scientific Agriculture / Life Science Research / Scientific Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Agriculture & Life Sciences Agriculture & Life Sciences First Name (required) 763346cb Last Name (required) db0a8e79 Email (required) 21dde7f6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) d1fec2d0 Last Name (required) 34773cd8 Email (required) f05d0e2d Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to avai