    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-operations-research-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Operations Research",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Operations Research - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor - Operations Research - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor - Operations Research 537780 Blacksburg, Virginia Industrial and Systems Engineering Teaching & Research Faculty College of Engineering Faculty Position in the Grado Department of Industrial and Systems Engineering Virginia Tech – Assistant Professor, Operations Research The Grado Department of Industrial and Systems Engineering (ISE) at Virginia Tech invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, effective August 2027. We seek outstanding candidates in Operations Research with strong methodological and theoretical skills in stochastic operations research, including applied probability, stochastic modeling and optimization, simulation, and related areas, with applications in areas including but not limited to: AI-enabled decision-making in supply chains and healthcare, the interface between simulation and AI, and resilient or data-driven systems. We are seeking candidates motivated to contribute to a collegial, interdisciplinary community with a strong tradition of both fundamental and applied research as well as innovative teaching. The department currently has 42 full-time faculty members, including 34 tenured/tenure-track faculty and six additional instructional faculty. Eight faculty members are early investigator recipients, and numerous others have received international or national recognition. Academic programs and research in the department encompass Human Factors Engineering & Ergonomics, Management & Systems Engineering, Manufacturing Systems Engineering, and Operations Research. Candidates will thus have the opportunity to work with a broad range of departmental faculty, as well as with faculty in many other colleges, centers, and institutes at Virginia Tech, including the Institute for Advanced Computing (launched in 2025 in the greater Washington, D.C. area), the Commonwealth Cyber Initiative , the Fralin Biomedical Research Institute , the National Security Institute , VT MADE – the Center for Advanced Manufacturing, and the Virginia Tech Transportation Institute . The department is home to 660 undergraduate students, 120 master’s students, and 100 doctoral students. The undergraduate and graduate ISE programs are currently ranked sixth and ninth, respectively, by U.S. News & World Report. This position is located at Virginia Tech’s main campus in Blacksburg, VA - an area consistently ranked among the country’s best places to live. In addition, our graduate programs in the greater Washington, D.C. area offer unique proximity to government and industry partners, with four ISE faculty members located at our campus in Alexandria, VA. Additional information about the department is available at: www.ise.vt.edu . Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a School of Medicine , a graduate college of Veterinary Medicine , a Graduate School , and an Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, and numerous extension offices . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Tenure-track faculty are expected to initiate and develop externally-funded independent research that is nationally recognized, conscientiously mentor research-oriented graduate students, teach effectively at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and serve the university and their professional communities. The successful candidate will have a Ph.D. in industrial and systems engineering, operations research, or a closely related field; demonstrated potential to develop a sustainable externally-funded research program, publish in leading IE/OR/OM/MS journals, and produce research of the caliber recognized by major best-paper and publication awards; and an ability to contribute to the department’s teaching mission at both the graduate and undergraduate levels by teaching courses in probability, probabilistic operations research, with the potential to contribute to teaching needs in simulation. Candidates with demonstrated interest in collaborative research in areas represented by the department’s existing faculty; demonstrated ability and willingness to work collaboratively with faculty from a variety of disciplines to expand disciplinary boundaries to address complex technical and societal challenges; recognition of research excellence as measured by awards; and instructional experience in higher education will receive strong consideration. Applicants must apply online at jobs.vt.edu (posting number 537780). Application materials include a cover letter, CV, up to three relevant research publications, and contact information for at least three professional references. In addition, applicants must provide three separate statements (up to 3 pages each): 1) a research statement; 2) a statement of teaching and mentoring philosophy; and 3) a statement expressing the candidate’s ideas for supporting an educational environment consistent with the Virginia Tech Principles of Community - specific examples of experiences, activities, and plans will help us identify candidates who can support and extend our university’s commitment to inclusive excellence. Review of applications will commence on November 16, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding the position should be directed to the Search Chair Dr. Xi Chen, who can be reached at isesearch@vt.edu . Candidates attending the INFORMS Annual Meeting may contact this email to request a meeting with a VT faculty member to learn more about the position, department, college, and university. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Devin Norris at dnorris11@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the on-campus interview. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 0ec0c083 Last Name (required) 46948224 Email (required) b4e17404 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert ef9b080c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Engineering Instructional / Teaching Faculty Engineering Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Engineering College of Engineering First Name (required) e2c55f42 Last Name (required) 0e7e9a8f Email (required) 202c9668 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 5a9d2903 Last Name (required) 2021025b Email (required) 64993554 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Agricultural Technician-Suffolk, VA Suffolk Virginia Tidewater AREC Virginia Tech's Tidewater Agricultural Research and Extension Center (AREC) is seeking a dedicated and detail-oriented Research Technician to assist our dynamic field crops agronomy and soybean research program. This is an off-campus, part-time position located at our facility in Suffolk, Virginia. You will work under the direction of the Agricultural Supervisor to support the lifecycle of small-plot agricultural research, from seed packaging to precision planting, field data collection, and post-harvest quality analysis. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - Northampton Machiponogo, Virginia Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for Northampton County. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - York County Yorktown Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for York County. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a senior management"
