    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/geospatial-analyst-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Geospatial Analyst",
      "description": "Geospatial Analyst - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Geospatial Analyst - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Geospatial Analyst 538163 Blacksburg, Virginia Fish and Wildlife Conservation Research Faculty Natural Resources Job Description The Virginia Tech Conservation Management Institute (CMI) seeks a highly motivated Geospatial Analyst to support geospatial data development, analysis, and management efforts associated with natural resource conservation and military land management programs. The successful candidate will develop, maintain, analyze, and document geospatial datasets using GIS, GPS, remote sensing technologies, and field-collected data to support research, planning, and project-critical decision making. Required Qualifications • MS Degree in natural resources or BS degree with applicable certifications directly related in Geography, Ecology, Forestry, Environmental Science, Natural Resources, GIS, Remote Sensing, or a related field. • Experience developing and analyzing geospatial datasets derived from aerial imagery, satellite imagery, LiDAR, and other remote sensing technologies. • Demonstrated ability to create professional cartographic products for technical reports, peer review publications and professional presentations. • Experience with GPS technologies and Esri GIS software. • Demonstrated experience collecting, managing, and integrating field and spatial data. • Must be familiar with and have the ability to develop spatial data sets that are compliant with Department of War Spatial Data Standards for Facilities, Infrastructure, and Environment. Preferred Qualifications • Experience supporting natural resource management on military installations. • Experience working with Department of Defense geospatial data standards and environmental programs. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Hours per week 40 Salary Range Starting at $60,000; commensurate with experience Review Date 10/23/2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Kelsey Lester at kdlester@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) ce1570b4 Last Name (required) 78c9521c Email (required) a23e5c49 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 04f06736 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Natural Resources Research / Scientific Natural Resources Research / Scientific Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Natural Resources Natural Resources First Name (required) 7e93807a Last Name (required) 8157986d Email (required) 8049863b Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 5a9a00f2 Last Name (requ