    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-associate-blacksburg-virginia-united-states-32787227-c149-4ad2-b827-308eb906583e": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Postdoctoral Associate - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Postdoctoral Associate 538175 Blacksburg, Virginia School of Plant & Environmental Sci Research Faculty Agriculture & Life Sciences Job Description The School of Plant and Environmental Sciences at Virginia Tech is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Associate to join an interdisciplinary research team working on innovative approaches to soil hydraulic characterization, environmental sensing, and hydrologic modeling. The position will support a USDA-NRCS funded project focused on improving soil hydraulic characterization through novel sensing, modeling, and data integration. The successful candidate will collaborate with faculty members in the Environmental Soil Science group and integrate field observations, sensor networks, remote sensing data, and process-based models to improve understanding of soil-water dynamics, root water uptake, drought resilience, and ecosystem responses to climate variability. The candidate will be expected to disseminate their work through presentations at annual meetings and publications in peer-reviewed journals. The postdoctoral associate is expected to train and supervisor work completed by students and research assistants involved in the project. General maintenance of laboratory facility and equipment. Required Qualifications • PhD must be awarded no more than four years prior to the effective date of the appointment with a minimum of one year eligibility remaining in Soil Science, Environmental Science, Civil and Environmental Engineering, or a closely related field. • Demonstrated experience in quantitative analysis of soil-water processes. • Strong computational and data analysis skills using R, Python, MATLAB, or related platforms. • Record of peer-reviewed publications commensurate with career stage. • Effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications • Experience with soil hydraulic characterization, infiltration measurements, soil moisture monitoring, or environmental sensor networks. • Experience with hydrologic, ecohydrological, or vadose zone modeling (e.g., HYDRUS, SWAT, ParFlow, or related models). •Experience acquiring, processing, and analyzing environmental data from proximal and remote sensing technologies. • Ability to work effectively within an interdisciplinary research team. • Demonstrated interest in developing independent research directions and pursuing external funding opportunities. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information $53,550 - $65,029; commensurate with experience Hours per week 40 Review Date 11/01/2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Dr. Huijie Gan at juijiegan@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) dac3992f Last Name (required) 79b2d1fd Email (required) e0d229fc Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 49399a83 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture / Life Science Research / Scientific Agriculture / Life Science Research / Scientific Loca