    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-of-wildlife-extension-blacksburg-virginia-united-states-48e2ed5d-dd8d-44ce-83ff-7d613e931201": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Wildlife Extension",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Wildlife Extension - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant/Associate Professor of Wildlife Extension - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant/Associate Professor of Wildlife Extension 537663 Blacksburg, Virginia Fish and Wildlife Conservation Teaching & Research Faculty Natural Resources Job Description The Department of Fish and Wildlife Conservation in the College of Natural Resources and Environment at Virginia Tech invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Wildlife Extension. This position will provide statewide leadership at the intersection of wildlife science, applied research, extension education, and public engagement. The faculty member will connect Virginia Tech research with Virginia Cooperative Extension, wildlife management agencies, landowners, local governments, agricultural producers, natural resource professionals, and communities across the Commonwealth. Priority program areas could include wildlife health and wildlife-vectored diseases, human-wildlife conflict/coexistence, deer and bear management, invasive and exotic wildlife, habitat conservation in rapidly changing landscapes, and public understanding of wildlife conservation and sustainable use. Position Expectations The anticipated allocation is 50% extension, 35% research, 10% teaching, and 5% service. The extension program is expected to include an assessment of stakeholder needs and the development of programming and materials to address these needs such as, statewide workshops, webinars, field days, landowner trainings, agent professional development, publications, decision-support tools, and digital resources, and ultimately documenting the impact of programming. The faculty member will work closely with Virginia Cooperative Extension specialists, Agriculture and Natural Resource agents and partners such as the Virginia Department of Wildlife Resources, United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) - Wildlife Services, Virginia Department of Forestry, non-governmental organizations (NGOs), and local governments. The successful candidate will establish a competitive, externally funded, applied research program that supports graduate students. The faculty member will submit competitive proposals beginning in the first year, pursue appropriate capacity and external funds, develop collaborations across the university, and produce peer-reviewed publications, extension scholarship, conference presentations, and impact reports. The faculty member will teach a 0:1 course load with teaching focused on FIW 4454 Human-Wildlife Conflicts and Coexistence, anticipated annually in the spring, and will contribute to graduate education and mentoring through applied research and extension scholarship. Required Qualifications • Ph.D. in wildlife science, human dimensions of wildlife, natural resources, ecology, extension education, or a closely related field by appointment start date. • Demonstrated expertise relevant to wildlife management, human-wildlife conflict and coexistence, wildlife health, habitat management, or human dimensions. • Evidence of ability to develop and deliver research-based educational programs for professional and public audiences. • Evidence of strong potential for externally funded applied research. • Demonstrated effectiveness in verbal and written communication, including a peer-reviewed publication record. Preferred Qualifications • Experience working with Cooperative Extension, state or federal wildlife agencies, landowners, local governments, or stakeholder organizations. • Graduate student mentoring experience. • For appointment at Associate Professor, a record of sustained scholarly productivity, strong record of external funding, and extension or engagement leadership commensurate with rank. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Hours per week 40 Review Date 10/15/2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. Applicants should submit: 1) Cover letter describing their interest in the position 2) Curriculum vitae 3) A 1-2 page statement describing their extension or professional program as appropriate to the position 4) A 1-2 page statement describing their research program 5) A 1-2 page statement describing their teaching and mentoring approach and how the candidate would tie all three missions together as a programmatic theme 6) Names and contact information for three professional references Additional materials may be requested as the search progresses. Inquiries should be addressed to the Search Committee Chair, with an email header that reads WILDLIFE EXTENSION POSITION: Dr. Elizabeth A. Hunter Assistant Unit Leader and Assistant Professor USGS Virginia Cooperative Fish and Wildlife Research Unit Department of Fish and Wildlife Conservation Virginia Tech Email: ehunter1@vt.edu About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Kelsey Lester at kdlester@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) e03d1c36 Last Name (required) e92242c1 Email (required) 69fbfa06 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 166f7efb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Natural Resources Instructional / Teaching Faculty Natural Resources Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Natural Resources Natural Resources First Name (required) de5696f7 Last Name (required) cf5fb279 Email (required) 78298d7c Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 8373b6e1 Last Name (required) aca3188f Email (required) e64ea6ed Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Agricultural Technician-Suffolk, VA Suffolk Virginia Tidewater AREC Virginia Tech's Tidewater Agricultural Research and Extension Center (AREC) is seeking a dedicated and detail-oriented Research Technician to assist our dynamic field crops agronomy and soybean research program. This is an off-campus, part-time position located at our facility in Suffolk, Virginia. You will work under the direction of the Agricultural Supervisor to support the lifecycle of small-plot agricultural research, from seed packaging to precision planting, field data collection, and post-harvest quality analysis. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - Northampton Machiponogo, Virginia Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for Northampton County. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - York County Yorktown Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for York County. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Please choose a senior management"
