    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/senior-faculty-position-in-cancer-research-virginia-tech-washington-dc-washington-dc-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Faculty Position in Cancer Research Virginia Tech- Washington DC",
      "description": "Senior Faculty Position in Cancer Research Virginia Tech- Washington DC - Washington DC, United States Senior Faculty Position in Cancer Research Virginia Tech- Washington DC - Washington DC, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Senior Faculty Position in Cancer Research Virginia Tech- Washington DC 537713 Washington DC Fralin Biomedical Res. Institute Teaching & Research Faculty Vice President for Research Job Description Virginia Tech’s (VT) Fralin Biomedical Research Institute (FBRI) is recruiting for an exceptional investigator in cancer research at the level of Professor or Associate Professor. The successful candidate will have a strong record of independently funded basic or translational cancer research, along with demonstrated commitment to faculty mentorship. This new position is part of a major research initiative by the Virginia Tech’s FBRI and will be located in our new facility based at the Children’s National Research and Innovation Campus in Washington DC ( fbri.vt.edu/dc ). Faculty at the DC campus have particular interest in precision oncology, cancer genomics, immunotherapy, neuro-oncology, and hematological malignancies. Applicants should have an earned doctorate (PhD, MD, and/or DVM), postdoctoral research experience, at least five years as faculty or equivalent, a record of accomplishment and research productivity through high-quality publications, with sustained and current extramural funding. The successful candidate will primarily be expected to maintain a high-quality, extramurally-funded cancer research program. They will also have the opportunity to participate in some teaching of graduate students and to serve as a research mentor for VT graduate, medical and undergraduate students. Appropriately qualified candidates may additionally be considered for the role of deputy director of the FBRI Cancer Research Center - DC. Competitive salary, space, and start-up package will be provided. Required Qualifications Applicants should have an earned doctorate (PhD, MD, and/or DVM), postdoctoral research experience, at least five years as faculty or equivalent, a record of accomplishment and research productivity through high-quality publications, with sustained and current extramural funding. The successful candidate will primarily be expected to maintain a high-quality, extramurally-funded cancer research program. Preferred Qualifications Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information Commensurate with Experience Hours per week 40+ Review Date 10/16/2026, but will remain open until filled. Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Brittany Shelton at sheltb@vtc.vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 2c933649 Last Name (required) 1324df82 Email (required) c8fe7f3e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert acffc106 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research / Scientific Research / Scientific Locations Washington DC Washington DC Senior Management Vice President for Research Vice President for Research First Name (required) a36d0005 Last Name (required) 49f41919 Email 