    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/department-head-materials-science-and-engineering-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Department Head - Materials Science and Engineering",
      "description": "Department Head - Materials Science and Engineering - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Department Head - Materials Science and Engineering - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Department Head - Materials Science and Engineering 538091 Blacksburg, Virginia Materials Science & Engineering Teaching & Research Faculty College of Engineering Job Description The Department of Materials Science and Engineering (MSE) in the College of Engineering at Virginia Tech invites applications and nominations for the position of Department Head. The successful candidate will be appointed as a tenured professor and a named professorship distinction is available. The selected Department Head will provide visionary, collaborative, and accountable leadership for a department with a strong tradition of research, education, and industry engagement. The Department Head serves as a member of the College of Engineering leadership team reporting to the Dean and is the department’s principal advocate to university leaders, alumni, industry, government sponsors, professional communities, and other external partners. The Department Head will lead the development and execution of a shared strategic vision with departmental faculty; foster excellence in research, education, mentoring, service, and outreach; steward departmental fundraising for resources; and build a culture in which faculty, staff, and students can thrive. The next Department Head will build on MSE’s distinctive strengths in hands-on education, materials innovation, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Priority opportunities include advancing research, graduate education, and undergraduate education; growing undergraduate and graduate enrollment; strengthening industry, national laboratories, and alumni partnerships; broadening the department’s visibility and impact; supporting faculty and staff success; and positioning MSE for leadership in advanced manufacturing, energy, microelectronics, health, national security, and sustainable materials. About the Department The Virginia Tech MSE department offers B.S., M.S., M.Eng., and Ph.D. degrees and is home to more than 20 faculty members whose expertise spans the development, manufacturing, characterization, testing, and application of advanced materials systems. Our research and educational programs encompass metals, ceramics and glasses, polymers, composites, electronic and optical materials, biomaterials, nuclear materials, nanomaterials, and computational materials science. The department is in the midst of an exciting period of growth and transformation as we redefine what materials science and engineering education, research, and impact should look like for the next generation of materials scientists and engineers. Building on our broad technical foundation, we are shaping a department positioned to address emerging challenges in energy, computing, national security, advanced manufacturing, sustainability, and other rapidly evolving areas where materials innovation will be essential. MSE’s students benefit from a close-knit learning environment, extensive laboratory experiences, undergraduate research, internships and cooperative education, and a distinctive Engineering Communications Program. Faculty and students engage in fundamental and applied collaborative research across the university, with industry, and with government partners. The MSE department is based in Holden Hall and has specialized characterization, processing, and synthesis laboratories as well as computational facilities in Hancock Hall, Whittemore Hall, the Virginia Tech Corporate Research Center (CRC), and the Kroehling Advanced Materials Foundry. These facilities support research, teaching, and engagement across the materials lifecycle. MSE also maintains a strong connection with Virginia Tech MADE, the university’s center for advanced manufacturing, which brings together strengths in advanced materials, computational design, manufacturing technologies, data analytics, and cyber-infrastructure. In addition, the department has strong connections with the VT Center for Photonics and Macromolecules Innovation Institute, as well as robust interdisciplinary connections to many departments across multiple colleges at VT. The department is home to the Green Engineering Program. Virginia Tech is a public land-grant university committed to teaching and learning, research, and outreach in the Commonwealth of Virginia and beyond. The university’s motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), guides its commitment to service, inclusive excellence, and public impact. The main campus is located in Blacksburg, Virginia in the New River Valley, offering an exceptional environment for professional and personal life. Leadership Responsibilities •Articulate and implement, with the department community, a compelling and actionable strategic vision aligned with the College of Engineering and Virginia Tech. •Advance a culture of excellence, collegiality, belonging, transparency, professionalism, and shared responsibility among faculty, staff, and students. •Build a connected and high-trust departmental community through visible, approachable, inclusive, and transparent leadership; develop shared ownership and emerging leaders across the faculty and staff; and make timely, accountable decisions that advance agreed-upon priorities. •Provide effective academic and administrative leadership for personnel, promotion and tenure, mentoring, budget and resource management, facilities, and departmental operations. •Champion high-quality, innovative undergraduate and graduate education, including hands-on learning, communication skills, student recruitment, retention, and career success. •Strengthen the department’s research enterprise, support interdisciplinary initiatives, and grow partnerships and resources through industry engagement, alumni relations, philanthropy, and sponsored research. •Expand external resources through strategic partnerships with industry, alumni, government, and philanthropic supporters, while raising MSE’s visibility as a university and national hub for materials science and engineering. •Represent and strongly advocate for MSE effectively within the College, university, professional communities, and external stakeholder networks. •Recruit, retain, develop, and recognize outstanding faculty and staff; promote the success and well-being of all members of the department. Required Qualifications •Ph.D. in materials science and engineering or a closely related field. •Demonstrated academic, administrative, or equivalent leadership experience, including the ability to set priorities, make sound decisions, and lead change. •Professional accomplishments and experience consistent with appointment as a tenured Professor in the Department of Materials Science and Engineering at Virginia Tech. Preferred Qualifications •A record of building consensus, communicating clearly and transparently, and bringing diverse perspectives together around shared goals. •Success in mentoring faculty, staff, and students and in developing collaborative, high-performing teams. •Experience with financial and personnel management, strategic planning, fundraising, and/or stewardship of complex academic or research operations. •Commitment to fostering a respectful, inclusive, and supportive community. •Evidence of productive partnerships with industry, government, alumni, professional organizations, and/or interdisciplinary research communities. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information Commensurate with Experience Hours per week 40 plus Review Date December 1, 2026 - open until filled Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Amy Hill at amyhill@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) dd432e2b Last Name (required) 48008ff5 Email (required) 45b5dd1f Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 1e4daf4e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Engineering Engineering Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Engineering College of Engineering First Name (required) 3abd70d4 Last Name (required) ee3ebeaf Email (required) f4a82a4c Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) d00bc419 Last Name (required) 0025d9a7 Email (required) 4527063f Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link