      "description": "Assistant / Associate Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant / Associate Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant / Associate Professor 537878 Blacksburg, Virginia Finance, Insurance & Business Law Teaching & Research Faculty College of Business Job Description The Pamplin College of Business at Virginia Tech invites applications for two tenure-track positions in the Department of Finance, Insurance and Business Law at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor (with tenure). These positions present an exciting opportunity to join a dynamic and growing department. Rank will be based on experience and record of achievement. The positions are based in Blacksburg, VA with an expected start date of August 2027. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis beginning immediately. For full consideration, applications should be submitted by November 20, 2026; review will continue until the positions are filled. Required Qualifications • Successful candidates should possess a doctoral degree in finance or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution by August 10, 2027 • Candidates for the rank of Assistant Professor must exhibit the potential to publish in top-tier finance and finance-related journals • Candidates for the rank of Associate Professor must possess an outstanding academic record, including publications in top-tier finance and finance-related journals and evidence of national/international recognition • Evidence of teaching effectiveness • Strong communication and interpersonal skills Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information Commensurate upon experience. Hours per week Varies Review Date November 20, 2026; open until filled. Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Jessica Linkous at jessrae@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) c854769b Last Name (required) fe3c4366 Email (required) 8afbbdf4 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 2bad9bfc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Instructional / Teaching Faculty Business / Accounting / Finance Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Business College of Business First Name (required) cd0cc553 Last Name (required) 838983ad Email (required) 7ac19376 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 30e519c8 Last Name (required) 5db7a217 Email (required) f73e05af Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available