    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-director-msba-programs-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, MSBA Programs",
      "description": "Assistant Director, MSBA Programs - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant Director, MSBA Programs - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Director, MSBA Programs 537909 Blacksburg, Virginia Dean of Business Teaching & Research Faculty College of Business Job Description We are seeking a dynamic, entrepreneurial-minded applicants for a professional faculty position as Assistant Director dedicated to teaching, student engagement, and corporate outreach. Responsibilities include leadership and direction of multiple graduate Master of Science in Business Administration (MSBA) programs/tracks (e.g., MSBA-BA, FIN) including budgeting/tracking of expenditures, marketing/recruitment of new students, teaching in the MSBA program; supervising and evaluating capstone analytics projects; interfacing with corporate capstone sponsors; and soliciting new capstone projects from prospective sponsors. The candidate will provide additional program support activities such as mentoring MSBA students, coaching graduate students in improving their communication skills when writing resumes, cover letters, consulting reports, and giving business presentations; and maintaining strategic relationships with corporate sponsors to maintain and enhance financial support of MSBA academic activities. The position is based in Blacksburg. Required Qualifications •A Master’s degree or PhD in business or a technical field •Excellent communication skills and proven training / teaching ability •Proven leadership or management experience with leadership in academic programs preferred •Strong public speaking / presentation skills •Proven customer interface skills in a project execution role, business development role, or both •Excellent interpersonal skills, and the ability to manage multiple and competing priorities in a dynamic environment Preferred Qualifications •Industry/business experience in consulting / government contracting, project management, or business intelligence and analytics •Experience planning, executing, and evaluating corporate and/or capstone projects •Prior senior leadership or executive leadership is a plus •Project and program management experience •Skills with specific analytics software or tools typically used in industry •General management experience Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information starting at $120,000; commensurate with experience Hours per week 40 Review Date October 16, 2026; open until filled Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Samantha Gagnet at sgagnet@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) b4784a2d Last Name (required) db929a59 Email (required) 11c7bdb3 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert be8e42e2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Instructional / Teaching Faculty Business / Accounting / Finance Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Business College of Business First Name (required) 7be5d17b Last Name (required) cafd