    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-of-practice-in-packaging-systems-and-design-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice in Packaging Systems and Design",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice in Packaging Systems and Design - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice in Packaging Systems and Design - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice in Packaging Systems and Design 537983 Blacksburg, Virginia Sustainable Biomaterials Teaching & Research Faculty Natural Resources Job Description The Department of Sustainable Biomaterials invites applications for the position of Professor of Practice at the Assistant or Associate level, in Packaging Systems and Design (PSD). We seek an accomplished packaging professional and educator who will provide essential instructional leadership, expand experiential and international education, strengthen industry partnerships, and prepare students for careers in the rapidly evolving packaging sector. The position is proposed as 75% teaching, 10% applied scholarship/industry engagement, and 15% service and will play a central role in the departmental coordination for internships (PSD Bridge Experience) and industry-sponsored capstone activities. Teaching and Mentoring Expectations The faculty member will carry a 3:3 teaching load and coordinate the PSD Bridge Experience. Initial teaching will include SBIO 2004 Computer-Aided Design in Packaging in fall and spring, SBIO 4054 Packaging Practicum in fall and spring, and SBIO 3954 Culture, History and Environment study abroad. During the first two years, the faculty member will develop a new advanced computer-aided design course and is expected to assume leadership of study abroad experiences, including those in Ireland and Australia/New Zealand. Teaching should integrate emerging technologies, including the responsible use of artificial intelligence, into structural design and capstone problem-solving. Research, Scholarship, Extension, and Engagement Expectations The position does not require a traditional independent research program. Applied scholarship will center on leading an industry-funded undergraduate capstone model, presenting project outcomes at professional or national conferences, and developing sustained relationships with packaging industry associations and employers. The faculty member will use professional networks to expand internship opportunities, sponsored projects, mentoring, and career opportunities for students. Required Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree in packaging science/engineering, industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, wood science, sustainable biomaterials, or a closely related field by appointment start date. • Several years of industrial or applied professional experience in packaging systems, design, CAD, product development, or related areas. • Demonstrated ability to teach, mentor, or train students or professionals in applied settings. • Evidence of strong industry relationships and the ability to support experiential learning and career preparation. • Ability to travel nationally and internationally to support student travel Preferred Qualifications • Masters or Doctoral degree in packaging science/engineering, industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, wood science, sustainable biomaterials, or a closely related field by appointment start date. • Experience with packaging CAD, structural design, capstone or sponsored-project instruction, and emerging AI-enabled design workflows. • Experience leading international or study-abroad education. • Engagement with professional organizations such as ISTA, PMMI, IoPP, or the Sustainable Packaging Coalition. • Experience developing industry-sponsored educational projects or internship pipelines. • Experience with AI implementation in an educational format • Experience with AI use during the packaging development process • Professional credentials and certifications such as CPP, PDP, etc. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information $65-$75,000 for Assistant; $75-$85,000 for Associate Hours per week 40 Review Date November 1, 2026 Additional Information Applicants should submit the following documents: Cover letter describing their interest in the position (up to one page) Curriculum vitae Names and contact information for three professional references. Statement describing their teaching and mentoring approach (up to two pages) to include: Your approach to effective teaching and mentoring at the undergraduate level. Courses that you would offer to enhance the Packaging Systems and Design curriculum. How your expertise, interests, and goals would contribute to the Packaging Systems and Design program and its faculty community. The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Trish Colley at colleyp@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) b2e7893a Last Name (required) ed36024e Email (required) e06130ac Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert ab4ec077 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Natural Resources Instructional / Teaching Faculty Natural Resources Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Natura