    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-associate-alexandria-virginia-united-states-40976006-b543-4704-a35e-16b13b4c945b": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate - Alexandria, Virginia, United States Postdoctoral Associate - Alexandria, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Postdoctoral Associate 537881 Alexandria, Virginia Housing Research Center Research Faculty College of Engineering Job Description The Virginia Center for Housing Research (VCHR) at Virginia Tech seeks a Postdoctoral Associate to support and advance applied research focused on housing affordability, housing markets, housing policy, and housing program development. Working collaboratively with VCHR faculty, government agencies, nonprofit organizations, and other stakeholders, the successful candidate will contribute to research initiatives that inform housing-related decision-making at the local, regional, and state levels. The position will involve designing and executing applied housing research projects, including collecting, managing, and analyzing quantitative and qualitative data related to housing needs, market conditions, housing affordability, and policy interventions. Key responsibilities include conducting comprehensive literature reviews, evaluating housing policies and programs, and developing evidence-based analyses to support housing studies, affordable housing initiatives, and economic assessments. Required Qualifications Doctorate degree in urban planning or equivalent with dissertation on a housing topic. PhD must be awarded no more than four years prior to the effective date of appointment with a minimum of one year eligibility remaining. Background in data analytics and science, housing policies and programs, especially data and methods applicable in housing research, and experience conducting applied housing research. Demonstrated experience in • data compilation and analysis relevant to local housing programs and policies • translating housing data and research findings into clear written, visual, and oral communication for technical and non-technical audiences. • qualitative research methods and analysis, including interviews, focus groups, and content analysis. Preferred Qualifications Experience conducting local and regional housing needs assessments and market analyses. Familiarity with inclusionary zoning (affordable dwelling unit) incentive programs and economic analysis required to support program development. Experience in applied housing research with the ability to perform and improve the efficiency/effectiveness/efficacy of analysis and methods. Experience with data organization and cleaning, including programming skills required to scrape data from documents and websites. Skills and experience with Python, R, and Excel. Experience with and understanding of AI tools. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information $63,480 Hours per week 40 hours - regular schedule Review Date 10/09/2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Sara Phillips at Sara.Phillips@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) a41125c7 Last Name (required) 82c68115 Email (required) b185f070 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 4722d5fa Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to