    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant/Associate Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant/Associate Professor 537827 Blacksburg, Virginia Biological Sciences Teaching & Research Faculty College of Science Job Description The Department of Biological Sciences in the College of Science at Virginia Tech seeks applicants for two (2) tenure-track research and teaching positions at the Assistant/Associate Professor levels in the area of Molecular Microbiology. We seek microbiologists who employ molecular techniques to study and modify microorganisms, with special emphasis on bacteria, fungi, and/or their viruses. The ideal candidates’ research programs would examine fundamental phenomena within the American Society for Microbiology’s three focus areas: health, applied & environmental microbiology, and mechanism discovery. Potential research topics may include but are not limited to: fundamental biological questions using microbes as model systems, molecular mechanisms of bacterial or fungal pathogens, host-microbe interactions, systems analysis of microbes alone or in communities, synthetic biology, or the engineering of microbes. The successful candidates’ research should be able to sustain a long term extramurally funded program and complement existing strengths in the department and at Virginia Tech. The successful candidates will be capable of teaching courses focused on molecular microbiology, microbial genetics, microbial physiology and/or microbial pathogenesis. Advising and mentoring of both graduate and undergraduate students is expected. Participation in departmental, college, and university affairs and collaboration with faculty both within and across the university is strongly encouraged and expected. These may include the Center for Emerging, Zoonotic, and Arthropod-borne Pathogens (CeZAP) and other programs associated with the Fralin Life Sciences Institute or the Fralin Biomedical Institute . Graduate recruiting can be through the departmental Graduate Program as well as via university-level graduate programs including the Infectious Disease Interdisciplinary Graduate Education Program (ID IGEP), Molecular and Cellular Biology (MCB), and Genetics, Bioinformatics, and Computational Biology (GBCB). Required Qualifications ● Ph.D. in a relevant discipline (e.g., Microbiology, Biology, Molecular Biology). ● Demonstrated research accomplishments in the area of molecular microbiology. ● Demonstrated interest in developing and teaching courses in microbiology or closely related content areas. ● Demonstrated effectiveness in verbal and written communication. Preferred Qualifications ● Evidence of ability to work in teams, including with academics in other disciplines, state or federal agencies, NGOs, or private industry. ● Demonstrated ability to acquire research funding. ● Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence through experience and/or through training. ● Demonstrated record of collegial interactions across a broad range of communities. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information Commensurate with experience Hours per week 40 hours - exempt position Review Date November 1, 2026 Additional Information Inquiries should be addressed to the Search Committee Co-Chairs at VTMicroSearch@vt.edu . Dr. David Popham, Professor, Department of Biological Sciences and Dr. Bryan Hsu, Associate Professor, Department of Biological Sciences Virginia Tech, Blacksburg, VA 24061. The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. Required Application Materials: 1. Cover letter expressing statement of interest in the position (not to exceed 1 page); 2. Resume/CV; 3. Written statement (not to exceed 5 pages) describing: A) research experience and future plans (~3 pages); B) teaching and mentoring experience and philosophy (~1 page); and C) commitment to building a strong academic, professional, and collegial community (~1 page). 4. Names, titles, and full contact information for 3 professional references. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Dreama Price at dreama@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 1745efb3 Last Name (required) 8e7228f0 Email (required) 171e54bc Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert e36d444e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Research / Scientific Instructional / Teaching Faculty Research / Scientific Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Science College of Science First Name (required) 6b9e3005 Last Name (required) 35a967bd Email (required) d4c1e24c Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First N