    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-philosophy-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Philosophy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Philosophy - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor, Philosophy - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor, Philosophy 537782 Blacksburg, Virginia Philosophy Teaching & Research Faculty Liberal Arts and Human Sciences Job Description The Department of Philosophy at Virginia Tech invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position as an Assistant Professor in Philosophy to begin on August 10, 2027. The area of specialization (AOS) is Metaphysics and Epistemology (broadly construed), and the area of concentration (AOC) is open. The standard courseload is 2-2 and includes courses at the undergraduate and graduate (MA) level. Applicants must have a PhD in Philosophy by the time of appointment and a demonstrated record of excellence in research in and teaching of Metaphysics and Epistemology. While not a requirement, the department is also very interested in candidates with teaching interests in the history of philosophy. For more information about Philosophy at Virginia Tech, please visit: https://liberalarts.vt.edu/departments-and-schools/department-of-philosophy.html. Required Qualifications A PhD in Philosophy by the time of appointment An active and relevant research agenda Evidence of teaching excellence Application Materials and Deadline Screening of applications will begin November 15, 2026. For full consideration, all materials must be submitted prior to this date. Please submit: A CV A cover letter A research statement A writing sample Evidence of teaching excellence Names and contact information for 3 professional references Please direct questions to Dr. Kelly Trogdon, Search Committee Chair, Department of Philosophy, 401-A War Memorial Hall, Blacksburg, VA 24061 | Phone: (540) 231-0777 | Email: trogdon@vt.edu Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information The expected salary range is $73,000 – $83,000 per annum (9-month academic appointment), depending on experience Hours per week * Review Date November 15, 2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Jin Tian Acton at jaction3@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 5a495c64 Last Name (required) 9bf8f19c Email (required) 66a63743 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 0fec9ac3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Liberal Arts and Human Sciences Liberal Arts and Human Sciences First Name (required) 121478ad Last Name (required) 7e7921c1 Email (required) 566150d4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Than