    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-associate-blacksburg-virginia-united-states-68da683b-f3d9-4b8a-b304-d488afcda2cc": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Postdoctoral Associate - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Postdoctoral Associate 537776 Blacksburg, Virginia Aerospace and Ocean Engineering Research Faculty College of Engineering Job Description The Intelligent Design Optimization (IDOpt) lab and the Multidisciplinary Analysis and Design Center for Advanced Vehicles at the Kevin T. Crofton Department of Aerospace and Ocean Engineering at Virginia Tech invites applications for a Postdoctoral Associate to conduct research in advanced aircraft design, multidisciplinary design analysis and optimization (MDAO), and model-based systems engineering (MBSE). The successful candidate will contribute to a NASA-funded research program (University Leadership Initiative) developing methods and open-source computational tools for certification-driven aircraft design. The primary focus of this position will be the development and application of computational methods for aircraft conceptual design. The researcher will develop and integrate aircraft disciplinary models within MDAO workflows and investigate methods for incorporating certification considerations directly into aircraft design and optimization. The researcher will also contribute to the integration of MDAO with MBSE to enable requirements-driven aircraft design. This work will involve connecting aircraft requirements, architectures, geometry, analysis models, and optimization workflows so that changes in requirements can be traced through the aircraft design process and used to efficiently conduct new design and trade studies. The project will demonstrate these capabilities through aircraft design studies of increasing complexity, including electrified aircraft configurations. The successful candidate will work as part of a multi-institutional research team involving Virginia Tech, other universities, NASA, and aerospace industry partners. The candidate will also contribute to the development and release of open-source research software, preparation of peer-reviewed publications, presentation of research results, and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate researchers. Required Qualifications -Ph.D. in Aerospace Engineering or a closely related field by the time of appointment. -Ph.D. must have been awarded within the past four years with at least one year of eligibility remaining. -Demonstrated research experience in aircraft design, including conceptual or preliminary aircraft design, aircraft sizing, or multidisciplinary aircraft analysis. -Experience developing scientific computing or engineering analysis software in Python using object-oriented programming principles. -Experience developing or applying aircraft design and performance simulations that integrate three or more relevant disciplines, such as aerodynamics, propulsion, structures, flight dynamics, stability and control, controls, or powertrain systems. -Demonstrated ability to conduct independent research and contribute effectively within a collaborative, multidisciplinary research team. -Experience presenting technical research at an international aerospace or aviation conference, such as AIAA SciTech Forum or AIAA AVIATION Forum. -First-author publication in a peer-reviewed engineering or scientific journal. Preferred Qualifications -Experience with NASA OpenMDAO or similar multidisciplinary design analysis and optimization frameworks. -Experience with model-based systems engineering (MBSE) and associated methods and tools, including SysML and MagicDraw/Cameo. -Experience with hybrid-electric or electrified aircraft sizing and design, including propulsion and energy-system integration. -Experience with OpenVSP for aircraft geometry definition, modeling, or analysis. -Experience developing or integrating multidisciplinary aircraft analysis models involving three or more areas such as aerodynamics, propulsion, weights, structures, performance, stability and control, flight dynamics, or reliability. -Experience formulating and solving aircraft design optimization problems, particularly multidisciplinary or gradient-based optimization problems. -Experience developing research-quality software collaboratively using modern software-development practices. -Experience mentoring undergraduate or graduate researchers. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information 63,480-65,000 Hours per week 40 Review Date 10/05/2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Erin Wilson at erinwilson@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 0ca0dcd3 Last Name (required) e72ac199 Email (required) 66ce0eff Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert d2e7bf45 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Engineering Research / Scientific Engineering Research / Scientific Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Engineering College of Engineering First Name (required) 75389956 Last Name (required) 035cf8b0 Email (required) d26c7b96 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consen