    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-blacksburg-virginia-united-states-8f1849a9-b586-4c71-8859-4c49191da758": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor 537656 Blacksburg, Virginia Mathematics Teaching & Research Faculty College of Science Job Description The Department of Mathematics at Virginia Tech ( http://www.math.vt.edu/) invites applications for an Assistant Professor, tenure-track faculty position in the research area of mathematics education with a start date of August 10, 2027, at its Blacksburg, VA, campus. The successful candidate will conduct research in undergraduate mathematics education, with particular interest in research specialties that complement and add to the department's existing research strengths. Possible specialties include but are not limited to the following: the teaching and learning of undergraduate mathematics and/or graduate mathematics, the mathematical preparation of prospective teachers, and the teaching and learning of applied or computational mathematics. Job requirements include a Ph.D. in mathematics, mathematics education, or a closely related field, including the equivalent of 18 semester credit hours of graduate level mathematics, at the time of appointment; and an active research program in undergraduate mathematics education. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain a distinguished research program, including seeking and securing funding needed to support their research agenda, and to provide effective instruction and advising to a diverse population of undergraduate and graduate students. Successful candidates will be able to teach courses in graduate mathematics education research and undergraduate mathematics content or mathematics for prospective teachers. Additional responsibilities include continuing development of professional capabilities and scholarly activities, including travel to attend conferences and meetings, and participation in department, college, university, and professional service. This position builds on the Mathematics Department’s existing strengths and efforts to expand its national prominence in mathematics education research. The successful candidate will join a thriving mathematics education research group, housed in the Mathematics Department, which currently has three tenured faculty, a postdoc, and several graduate students enrolled in a Mathematics PhD program with a dissertation and coursework focus in educational research. Additionally, the mathematics education community at Virginia Tech includes two tenure-track faculty in the School of Education with a PhD program in Curriculum and Instruction. The two groups are highly collaborative, with joint research projects and a weekly seminar. Additionally, the College of Science has a Center for Advancing Undergraduate Science Education, which supports broader DBER efforts beyond mathematics. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to engage in interdisciplinary research, curriculum development, or outreach initiatives with other members of the Virginia Tech faculty. The Mathematics Department is committed to building a welcoming and supportive community of mathematical scientists through programs and activities woven into the department’s research, teaching, and outreach efforts. This commitment is illustrated by programs such as the following: Mathematics: Opportunities in Research and Education; activities organized by the Virginia Tech Chapter of the Association for Women in Mathematics (winner of the 2021 AWM Student Chapter Award for Scientific Excellence); and the Blacksburg Math Circle. Additionally, Virginia Tech is committed to supporting the success of its faculty members through policies that include the modification of duties, the extension of tenure clocks, mentoring, proposal-writing guidance, and dual-career accommodations, depending on individual circumstances. Interviewed candidates will meet with a work-life liaison for a confidential conversation about the details of these policies. The person appointed will have the following responsibilities: - Develop and maintain a distinguished research program in mathematics education research, including seeking and securing funding needed to support your research agenda; - Continually develop their own scholarly activities, professional capabilities, and service to the profession; - Provide effective instruction and advising to a diverse population of undergraduate and graduate students; - Teach courses in graduate mathematics education research and undergraduate mathematics content or mathematics for prospective teachers; - Participate actively and effectively in department and university administrative governance; and - Adhere to the responsibilities of the faculty as described by the faculty handbook ( https://faculty.vt.edu/faculty-handbook.html ). Required Qualifications To receive consideration, applicants must have: - a Ph.D. in mathematics, mathematics education, or a closely related field at the time of appointment with the equivalent of 18 semester credits of graduate level mathematics; and - an active research program in research in undergraduate mathematics education. Preferred Qualifications It is desired that candidates have: - a comprehensive record of achievement, commensurate with career stage; - a research program in mathematics education that compliments and adds to the department’s existing strengths; - vision, creativity, and initiative relevant to research and instruction; - evidence of viable research funding; and - demonstrated effectiveness or interest and potential in undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentoring. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information Commensurate with experience Hours per week 40 hours - exempt position Review Date October 23, 2026 Additional Information An online application is required. Please visit www.jobs.vt.edu , select “Apply Now,” and search by posting number 537656. Please include a cover letter, a CV, a research statement, a teaching statement, an (un)official transcript documenting the equivalent of 18 semester credits of graduate level mathematics, and a list of 3 references that will be contacted for those candidates that are being considered for a screening interview. Additional information about position requirements and responsibilities can be found at the following URLs: http://www.hr.vt.edu or https://www.math.vt.edu . The faculty handbook ( https://faculty.vt.edu/faculty-handbook.html ) gives a complete description of faculty responsibilities. Questions about the search may be addressed to: mathed2026@vt.edu. Applications received by 11:59 pm EST on October 23, 2026 will receive full consideration. The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. Some travel to meetings and conferences is required. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Sarah McDearis at sworl9@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) ace1e825 Last Name (required) 8095aeda Email (required) 96de2506 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 1df441ec Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Fa