    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/research-professorial-open-rank-position-spectrum-dominance-division-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Research Professorial Open Rank Position, Spectrum Dominance Division",
      "description": "Research Professorial Open Rank Position, Spectrum Dominance Division - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Research Professorial Open Rank Position, Spectrum Dominance Division - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Research Professorial Open Rank Position, Spectrum Dominance Division 537027 Blacksburg, Virginia VTNSI Research Faculty Vice President for Research Job Description The Virginia Tech National Security Institute (VTNSI) was formed in 2021 with the aspiration to become the nation’s preeminent academic organization at the nexus of interdisciplinary research, technology, policy, and talent development to advance national security. The Institute grew from the Hume Center, which was launched in 2010 thanks to an endowment from Ted and Karyn Hume. VTNSI is a national leader in advancing security and resilience through innovative and applied research, empowering the next generation of experts, and building strategic alliances to address evolving national security challenges. We bring together exceptional interdisciplinary faculty, unique research infrastructure, and deep partnerships with industry and government sponsors to execute impactful research and development. The Spectrum Dominance Division seeks a Research Assistant Professor, Research Associate Professor, or Research Professor at its office in Blacksburg, Virginia. The Spectrum Dominance Division (SDD) within VTNSI is home to 30 full-time faculty researchers with focus areas in electrical engineering, computer engineering, computer science, and applied mathematics. SDD’s portfolio reaches across all aspects of the radio frequency transmit/receive chain, including antenna and phased array design, baseband waveform design, and receiver design. SDD houses domain expertise in SDR development, AI/ML applied to the radio frequency (RF) spectrum (i.e., RFML), SIGINT, RADAR, cellular, electromagnetic materials, cognitive radio, and additive manufacturing. The hiring rank of this position will be based on the candidates' background and experience. While engaging in cutting-edge RF research, SDD has a particular focus on TRL 3-6 R&D, acting as the bridge from fundamental research on campus to prototypes for government and commercial sponsors. A particular strength is real-time RF system development leveraging in-house FPGA, GPU, and SDR platforms. Importantly, SDD has successfully transitioned multiple capabilities for real-time RF machine learning, automotive cybersecurity, and radar threat warning models. Validation of SDD products is accomplished in VTNSI’s state-of-the-art 5,000 sq. ft. of wireless testing and lab spaces as well as the Counter-UAS Testing and Research Center (CTRC), between them housing SDR testbeds, two RF anechoic chambers, and high-end measurement equipment (e.g. spectrum analyzers, vector network analyzers, etc.) supporting bands up to 110 GHz. These capabilities complement a nearly $10M investment in secure computing infrastructure, housing expansive GPU and CPU clusters. Motivated applicants are sought to help continue to build SDD’s radio frequency portfolio and will be expected to: · Lead the direction and technical execution of sponsored programs to achieve stated sponsor deliverables. · Disseminate program outputs into technical documents, publish peer-reviewed academic papers, and/or open-source codebases/datasets/etc. · Support business development efforts to secure new sponsored research programs. · Support program execution as needed. Additionally, applicants will have the opportunity to: · Mentor undergraduate student teams engaged in experiential learning programs. · Obtain a courtesy appointment in a relevant academic department to: · Co-advise Master’s and PhD students alongside tenured faculty within relevant academic departments. · Occasionally teach relevant courses within the department. Required Qualifications · An earned Doctorate degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, or related field. · Evidence of high potential for excellence in research and development as demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications and/or open-source codebases. · Scholarship and funding credentials that support the rank of either research assistant professor, research associate professor, or research professor. · Proficiency with the software/hardware tools germane to the applicant’s field of research. · Demonstrated ability to work as a member of a team in scoping and executing research projects. · Given the nature of the research conducted and the requirements from federal sponsors, the candidate must be a U.S. citizen. · Ability and willingness to obtain and maintain a security clearance. Preferred Qualifications · Active security clearance at the TS/SCI level. · Experience writing grant and contract proposals. · Experience serving as principal investigator on research grants and contracts (required for ranks of research associate professor and research professor). · Interest and/or experience in working effectively with academic faculty, staff and student populations. · Experience with research programs supporting defense and intelligence community sponsors. · Experience with research programs involving communications system prototype development and demonstration, with an emphasis on 5G/6G/O-RAN protocols, radio frequency artificial intelligence and machine learning, software-defined radios, and digital signal processing. · Experience or technical expertise in counter-UAS technologies including detection, tracking, and identification, as well as mitigation or UAS countermeasures using communications and/or RADAR signatures. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information $130,000 - 200,000; commensurate with experience and research professorial rank offered Hours per week 40 hours per week Review Date October 5, 2026 Additional Information Due to the nature of the Institute's work, all candidates must be US citizens and have the ability to obtain and maintain a security clearance. The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact VTNSI Human Resources at nsihr@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) b87a65e6 Last Name (required) 76914613 Email (required) 219499d9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 64d0cfd9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Engineering Research / Scientific Engineering Research / Scientific Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Vice President for Research Vice President for Research First Name (required) 84d2afac Last Name (required) 888bc7e0 Email (required) 87c5033e Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 01a24bd0 Last Name (required) 940764c0 Email (required) 13fbc715 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Agricultural Technician-Suffolk, VA Suffolk Virginia Tidewater AREC Virginia Tech's Tidewater Agricultural Research and Extension Center (AREC) is seeking a dedicated and detail-oriented Research Technician to assist our dynamic field crops agronomy and soybean research program. This is an off-campus, part-time position located at our facility in Suffolk, Virginia. You will work under the direction of the Agricultural Supervisor to support the lifecycle of small-plot agricultural research, from seed packaging to precision planting, field data collection, and post-harvest quality analysis. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - Northampton Machiponogo, Virginia Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for Northampton County. Administrative & Fiscal Assistant - York County Yorktown Virginia Southeast District Coop. Extension Virginia Cooperative Extension is seeking an Administrative & Fiscal Assistant for York County. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any 