    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/open-rank-industrial-organizational-faculty-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Open Rank Industrial Organizational Faculty",
      "description": "Open Rank Industrial Organizational Faculty - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Open Rank Industrial Organizational Faculty - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Open Rank Industrial Organizational Faculty 537534 Blacksburg, Virginia Psychology Teaching & Research Faculty College of Science Job Description The Department of Psychology at Virginia Tech is seeking applicants with a specialization in Industrial-Organizational Psychology for an open-rank tenure-line position, at either the Assistant, Associate, or Full professor level (commensurate with experience). Successful applicants will be required to have a Ph.D. by the anticipated August 10, 2027 start date, a demonstrated commitment to and successful track-record appropriate to their rank in research, teaching and mentoring, and service and engagement, and show promise in securing future extramural funding to support their research program. The areas of research and teaching expertise within industrial-organizational psychology are open, although we are particularly interested in candidates who can align with broader department and university initiatives relevant to data science (e.g., machine learning, artificial intelligence, big data approaches to understanding organizations and work) and/or the intersection of industrial-organizational psychology and related fields such as occupational health (e.g., employee well-being, stress, workplace interventions, occupational safety). About the Department The Department of Psychology, housed within the College of Science at Virginia Tech, is a Carnegie Foundation R1 doctoral institution, and faculty members of the Department of Psychology are highly active scholars across a range of research areas (i.e., Industrial-Organizational, Clinical, and Cognitive Neuroscience and Behavior, Developmental), who work to increase understanding of psychological processes involved in human behavior (https://psyc.vt.edu). While faculty members in Psychology share a common interest in psychological processes, our specific interests, research methods, and expertise are diverse and include both behavioral and neuroscience approaches with experimental, survey, and big data methodologies. Some researchers are committed to increasing understanding of basic psychological processes, while others emphasize implications for developmental, organizational, and clinical issues. The Psychology Department offers a supportive environment, including a mentoring program for its junior faculty. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in psychology or a related field by August 10th, 2027 Preferred Qualifications Independence in growing an established and nationally recognized research program Strong potential for securing external research funding or evidence of funding for more senior candidates Evidence of effective contribution to teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses Prior experience and willingness to mentor students in research Service and engagement in the field of I/O Psychology Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information Commensurate with experience Hours per week 40+ exempt position Review Date 10/01/26 Additional Information 1) A curriculum vitae (include any pending, or under review, submissions) 2) A statement of research accomplishments and future research directions 3) A statement of teaching experience with evidence of effective teaching 4) Three samples of scholarly writing (published, in press, under review, or in progress). We recommend candidates submit the research they are most proud of, regardless of journal ranking or impact factor. 5) The names and contact information of three academic references (letters are not required initially) The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. The position does require some travel to meetings and conferences. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Michelle Wooddell at woodyaj@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) c760e5ef Last Name (required) e9d55681 Email (required) b380501e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert ca719d93 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Instructional / Teaching Faculty Research / Scientific Instructional / Teaching Faculty Research / Scientific Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Science College of Science First Name (required) a4502609 Last Name (required) aaca260f Email (required) 1a85b981 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) f031f6e5 Last Name (required) d5217dcf Email (required) c804884b Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and info