      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Practice - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Assistant Professor of Practice - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Professor of Practice 537311 Blacksburg, Virginia Accounting & Information Systems Teaching & Research Faculty College of Business Job Description The Department of Accounting and Information Systems in the R. B. Pamplin College of Business at Virginia Tech invites applications for a non-tenure track faculty position. Faculty hired for this position will be responsible for teaching 24 credit hours per year, further building the curriculum, and working closely with the business community. We seek candidates with expertise in taxation, who will contribute to the department’s mission through teaching, collaboration, and service. Professors of Practice are expected to engage with industry professionals and remain active in their profession in ways that contribute to their university assignments. Responsibilities include: • Teach and develop undergraduate and/or graduate courses within the Department of Accounting and Information Systems curriculum. • Provide academic leadership and mentorship within the department. • Contribute to departmental, college, and university service and governance. • Support the strategic growth and visibility of the department’s academic programs and initiatives. About the Department: The Department of Accounting and Information Systems (ACIS) at Virginia Tech is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and outreach. ACIS prepares students for successful professional careers through innovative academic programs. Faculty are recognized for producing impactful research that advances both academic scholarship and professional practice while maintaining strong partnerships with industry. Through active engagement with alumni, employers, and the accounting profession, ACIS provides students with exceptional experiential learning opportunities and a supportive community dedicated to developing the next generation of accounting and information systems leaders. Additional information about the department is available at https://acis.pamplin.vt.edu/. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in accounting or relevant field, or a Master's degree in accounting and professional licensure in an accounting related field (e.g., CPA, or other professional accounting certification) with equivalent years of accounting-related work experience at the time of application. This position will primarily be responsible for teaching courses in taxation. Significant teaching and/or professional experience in taxation is required. Preferred Qualifications Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information Commensurate with experience Hours per week 40 Review Date August 24, 2026 - open until filled Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Phyllis Neece at pneece@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 73786fb9 Last Name (required) d061531a Email (required) cdad5c99 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert c466a75f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your