    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-associate-ai-tools-for-research-administration-and-development-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate – AI Tools for Research Administration and Development",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate – AI Tools for Research Administration and Development - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Postdoctoral Associate – AI Tools for Research Administration and Development - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Postdoctoral Associate – AI Tools for Research Administration and Development 537218 Blacksburg, Virginia Research/Interdisc. Prog. - Admin Research Faculty Vice President for Research Job Description The Office of Research and Innovation at Virginia Tech invites applicants for a postdoctoral associate. We are seeking a well-qualified applicant who will engage stakeholders to explore opportunities for and develop a medium-term plan for using artificial intelligence tools to support research administration, strategy, and development. The candidate will work with stakeholders to understand opportunities and challenges faced by the research community and explore opportunities to use AI to meet those needs. Examples of opportunities that may emerge include reducing administrative load, improving faculty pre- and post-award service, strengthening compliance support, generating better research intelligence, and creating a scalable model for responsible AI use in research administration. The successful applicant will work closely with ORI Information Technology (IT), Electronic Research Administration (ERA), and Data & Analytics teams to develop and share best practices, understand available data and security challenges, build sustainable solutions, and provide expert perspective on using AI. Required Qualifications - PhD in computer science, statistics, data analytics, business administration, or related areas - PhD must be awarded no more than four years prior to the effective date of appointment with a minimum of one year eligibility remaining. - Experience developing sustainable, secure, AI-enabled solutions intended for end-user use. - Awareness of administrative or business processes and decision making - Experience working with and engaging stakeholders or customers to understand needs and requirements - Experience making medium- to long-term project plans - Strong communication skills Preferred Qualifications - Experience working with proprietary or sensitive financial and administrative data - Experience with process mapping and/or process improvement - Experience building solutions within policy, legal, and contractual requirements as part of a larger team Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information $60,000; commensurate with experience Hours per week 40+ Review Date August 12, 2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Lynn Byrd at byrd@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) b633410b Last Name (required) d19a38a7 Email (required) 81c1263c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert ca987488 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Data Analytics / Security Information Systems / Technology Research / Scientific Data Analytics / Security Information Systems / Technology Research / Scientific Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg