      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate - Alexandria, Virginia, United States Postdoctoral Associate - Alexandria, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Postdoctoral Associate 536793 Alexandria, Virginia Institute for Advanced Computing Research Faculty Greater Washington, D.C Area Job Description A postdoctoral associate is sought to conduct research in the area of integrated circuits at Virginia Tech's Institute for Advanced Computing with an appointment in the Bradley Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering. The Postdoc will particularly participate in the design and development of integrated system-on-chips for wireless sensing, communication, and implantable applications. The postdoctoral associate will be expected to: * Complete independent research in accordance with current ongoing research activities in the broad area of integrated circuits * Publish high-quality research in top international conferences and journals in the field * Provide leadership and project management for ongoing activities, including working with researchers in other fields of study and collaborators at other institutions * Participate in the preparation of grant proposals when needed, guided by their postdoc advisor * Complete other research-related duties, as assigned Required Qualifications - Completed or Expected to Complete a PhD in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or related areas. PhD must be awarded no more than four years prior to the effective date of appointment with a minimum of one year eligibility remaining. - An established track record of scholarly publications in high impact conferences and journals; - Demonstrated background and expertise in integrated circuits and experience with integrated circuit design tools such as Cadence - A track record of research publications in reputable conferences and journals - Effective communication and teamwork skills Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Hours per week 40 Review Date Ongoing, first review 7/10/2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or ap