    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/associate-professor-blacksburg-virginia-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Professor",
      "description": "Associate Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Associate Professor - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Associate Professor 533670 Blacksburg, Virginia Management Teaching & Research Faculty College of Business Job Description The Department of Management in the Pamplin College of Business at Virginia Tech seeks applications for one tenure-track faculty position to begin August 2026. This position is for the main campus in Blacksburg, Virginia. This search is specifically for an associate professor, tenured at a strong research institution, or an advanced assistant professor. This is an organizational behavior/human resources position. As such, we are particularly interested in candidates with strong research and teaching interests in organizational behavior and/or human resources. Ideal applicants will have demonstrated abilities in research and doctoral student mentorship and can contribute to the strong research culture of the Pamplin College of Business The Department of Management consists of 36 full-time faculty with an impressive range of leading-edge research and teaching expertise in various areas of management. Our tenure-track faculty include Jeffrey Arthur, Kiran Awate, Daniel Beal, William Becker, Katrina Brownell, Kevin Carlson, Cynthia Devers, Devi Gnyawali, Donald Hatfield, Richard Hunt, Pankaj Kumar, Trey Lewis, Christopher Porter, Karen Schnatterly, Phil Thompson, David Townsend, A.K. Ward Bartlett, and Marla White. Our faculty publish in top journals, including Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Journal of Applied Psychology, Journal of Business Venturing, Journal of International Business Studies, Journal of Management, Strategic Management Journal, Organization Science, and others . Virginia Tech has 30,000+ undergraduate and 7,000+ graduate students and a $1B+ Innovation Campus in Arlington VA ( https://www.vt.edu/innovationcampus/index.html ) that is key to continuing our development of world-class research and educational programs in management, entrepreneurship, and emerging area innovation. These initiatives are supported by a growing number of public/private partnerships sponsored by Virginia Tech, the Commonwealth of Virginia, high growth startups, and leading global companies. The Pamplin College of Business offers majors in management, accounting and information systems, business information technology, finance, hospitality and tourism management, marketing, and real estate. The Department of Management’s academic programs include four undergraduate majors, three interdisciplinary minors, and a full-time Ph.D. program. The department is an active contributor to five master’s programs, including the top-ranked Master of Information Technology Program, as well as an Executive Ph.D. program headquartered in the new 11-story, 300,000 square-foot Innovation Campus building in Alexandria, VA. Virginia Tech also recently opened the 1st building of the Global Business Analytics Complex on its main campus in Blacksburg, and groundbreaking for a 2nd building that will serve as the new home for the Pamplin College of Business will commence in September 2025. Required Qualifications Candidates should have: (1) a doctorate in Management, or a closely related field from an AACSB accredited or similar school; (2) a strong program of scholarly research focused on organizational behavior or human resources with recent publications in top management journals; (3) evidence of successful mentoring of doctoral students and/or junior faculty; (4) interest in continuing to conduct research with a high probability of publication in top management journals; and (5) the ability to contribute in meaningful ways to advancing the research visibility of the college and university. Preferred Qualifications Preferred candidates will have: (1) research that intersects the organizational behavior and human resources subfields; (2) overlap of research interests with those of our current faculty; and (3) demonstrated teaching effectiveness. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information Hours per week N/A Review Date 08/18/2025 Additional Information Virginia Tech’s Principles of Community are fundamental to the on-going efforts to increase access and inclusion and to create a community that nurtures learning and growth for all its members. We are committed to building a diverse faculty community and strongly encourage applications from candidates from various backgrounds. Virginia Tech is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Chelle Ferguson (chelled19@vt.edu) with any questions. Review of applications will begin August 18, 2025, and will continue until the position is filled. About Blacksburg Blacksburg is located near the Blue Ridge Mountains and the Appalachian Trail, and its natural beauty and temperate climate are attractive to many. Blacksburg is also ranked as one of the top places in America to raise children as it boasts high-quality K-12 schools and a relatively low cost of living. The greater Blacksburg area (Blacksburg, Christiansburg, Radford) has approximately 150,000 residents and is near Roanoke (population 100,000+) and the Roanoke-Blacksburg Regional Airport. Blacksburg is also located within driving distance to Charlotte (NC), Washington, D.C., Research Triangle Region (NC), the Port of Virginia in Norfolk, and Atlanta (GA). The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including the Innovation Campus in Northern Virginia; the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke; sites in Newport News and Richmond; and numerous Extension offices and research centers . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $500 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance . These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Chelle Ferguson at chelled19@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 5f724de4 Last Name (required) 74aaae96 Email (required) 6163c04b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 2b749949 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Instructional / Teaching Faculty Business / Accounting / Finance Instructional / Teaching Faculty Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Business College of Business First Name (required) 0a2b5134 Last Name (required) d1301df8 Email (required) ba98d5c0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 3b757c56 Last Name (required) 0847d313 Email (required) 4d9b81b6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree